@startuml
!theme toy
title Frame reservation and GPU credit lifecycle

state "Local\ncredit charged on main" as local #6CB4EE
state "Queued\naccepted by lane transport" as queued #77DD77
state "Submitted\nfence value V accepted" as submitted #FFB347
state "Quarantined\nsubmit possibly executed" as quarantined #FF6961
state "Released\ncredit returned" as released #B0B0B0

[*] --> local : admitClientFrame_
local --> queued : submitFrame accepted
local --> released : dropped or pre-submit error
queued --> submitted : result carries submit value V
queued --> released : lane drop, cancel,\nor never-applied result
submitted --> released : CPU settled and\nretirement frontier >= V
submitted --> quarantined : submit fate unknown
quarantined --> [*] : teardown only
released --> [*]

note right of submitted
  Two independent milestones:
  CPU settlement (result drained)
  and GPU completion (fence V).
  The credit returns only when
  both hold.
end note

note bottom of local
  Two ledgers bound work at 2:
  Application reservations on main
  and Renderer credits on the lane.
  kMaxOutstandingFrames = 2
end note
@enduml
